<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>CUSV</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <description>
    Textron Systems Fleet-class Common Unmanned Surface Vessel (CUSV) --
    a real, currently-active US Navy mine-countermeasures / anti-submarine
    warfare USV. This project's model is NOT official Textron CAD (no
    public CAD exists) -- it is a physics-parameter model built from
    Textron's publicly disclosed dimensions/displacement (see Wikipedia's
    "Fleet-class unmanned surface vessel" page), with a simple primitive
    hull for visual reference only. Full derivation, disclosed assumptions,
    and disclosed simplifications are in model.sdf's header comment.

    Properties (sourced)

    Displacement: 7.7 tonnes (7700 kg)
    Length:       12 m (39 ft)
    Beam:         3.4 m (11.2 ft)
    Hull type:    semi-planing monohull
    Top speed:    35 kn (real vehicle; NOT reproduced in this simulation
                  -- see model.sdf header for why)

    ArduPilot

    Vehicle type:     Rover
    Frame type:       rover-skid (twin differential thrust, assumed
                       propulsion configuration -- see model.sdf header)

  </description>
</model>
